{"abstract":"Long-term exercise training elicits tremendous health benefits; however, the molecular understanding is incomplete and identifying therapeutic targets has been challenging. Rho GTPases are among the most regulated groups of proteins after exercise in human skeletal muscle, yet, unexplored candidates for mediating the effects of exercise training. We found that the Rho GTPase Rac1 was activated acutely after multiple exercise modalities in human skeletal muscle. Loss of Rac1 specifically in muscle attenuated contraction-induced muscle protein synthesis, diminished improvements in running capacity, and prevented muscle hypertrophy after exercise training in mice. Additionally, Ncf1∗ mice revealed that Rac1 regulated glycogen resynthesis via a NOX2-dependent mechanism. Molecularly, Rac1 was required for contraction-induced p38MAPK signaling towards HSP27, MNK1, and CREB phosphorylation. In vivo muscle-targeted overexpression of a hyperactive Rac1-mutant elevated reactive oxidant species production during exercise but did not affect muscle mass. Using mass spectrometry-based proteomics, we found that loss or gain of Rac1 muscle protein affected pathways related to cytoskeleton organization, muscle adaptation, and large ribosomal subunits. Thus, skeletal muscle Rac1 mediates both molecular and functional adaptation to exercise training.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Raun, Steffen Henning","Henriquez-Olguin, Carlos","Frank, Emma","Schlabs, Farina L","Hahn, Nanna Just","Knudsen, Jonas Roland","Ali, Mona Sadek","Andersen, Nicoline Resen","Møller, Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","Davey, Jonathan","Qian, Hongwei","Coelho, Ana","Carl, Christian Strini","Voldstedlund, Christian T.","Kiens, Bente","Holmdahl, Rikard","Gregorevic, Paul","Jensen, Thomas Elbenhardt","Deshmukh, Atul S.","Richter, Erik A.","Sylow, Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828708"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Chile","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","Universidad Finis Terrae","University of Melbourne"],"keyword":["Contraction","Exercise training","Glycogen","Metabolism","Muscle hypertrophy","Protein synthesis","Rac1","Skeletal muscle"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skeletal muscle rac000000000001 mediates exercise training adaptations towards muscle glycogen resynthesis and protein synthesis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.redox.2025.103844","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828708","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12418856","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40886619","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105014537995","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3d429d57-19e0-4fcf-bf4f-402d0ae9f0bb"],"keyword":["Contraction","Exercise training","Glycogen","Metabolism","Muscle hypertrophy","Protein synthesis","Rac1","Skeletal muscle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B607CAB5D8FC6AD2193B7BB56ECE4F1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.redox.2025.103844","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/463747989/Skeletal_muscle_Rac1_mediates.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Metabolism in Cancer and Ageing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cl","key":"universidad finis terrae","loc":["Chile","America, South","OECD"],"name":"Universidad Finis Terrae","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of melbourne","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Melbourne","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen H.","key":"raunpau","last":"Raun","locid":"c3f5e98f-b81f-4cde-b7dd-93c2d92dd26d","name":"Raun, Steffen Henning","name_org":"Raun, Steffen H.","orcid":"0000-0003-2050-505X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Carlos","key":"henriquezolguínpau","last":"Henriquez-Olguín","locid":"04949417-b244-43fb-b9f7-9e36174132bc","name":"Henriquez-Olguin, Carlos","name_org":"Henriquez-Olguín, Carlos","orcid":"0000-0002-9315-9365","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emma","key":"frankpau","last":"Frank","locid":"7bea739e-c158-4dac-a74b-0f6cb4ba88a6","name":"Frank, Emma","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Farina","key":"schlabspau","last":"Schlabs","locid":"7cbebce3-b9e3-4073-ab65-7a17c872c050","name":"Schlabs, Farina L","name_org":"Schlabs, Farina","orcid":"0009-0006-2614-1620","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nanna Just","key":"hahnpau","last":"Hahn","locid":"a5f7d9d5-9eee-4ff7-a7bd-1b36741d0fcc","name":"Hahn, Nanna Just","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Roland","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3bebd5f8-2b5c-4c65-9775-afe9e85d103a","name":"Knudsen, Jonas Roland","orcid":"0000-0002-5471-491X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mona S.","key":"alipau","last":"Ali","locid":"dff2ed58-7683-4e19-ab9b-6ccea6c69268","name":"Ali, Mona Sadek","name_org":"Ali, Mona S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1152-3256","rank":7,"rolecode":