 S.","key":"deshmukhpau","last":"Deshmukh","locid":"ec9031a8-0215-4c06-ba88-f66863916df9","name":"Deshmukh, Atul S.","orcid":"0000-0002-2278-1843","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik A.","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lykke","key":"sylowpau","last":"Sylow","locid":"f86d592e-fb11-4ec7-a7b4-d63eb53f94c8","name":"Sylow, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-0905-5932","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40886619"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.redox.2025.103844","issn":["22132317"],"journal":"Redox Biology","paperid":"103844","status":"p","title":"Redox Biology","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105014537995"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3d429d57-19e0-4fcf-bf4f-402d0ae9f0bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Skeletal muscle Rac1 mediates exercise training adaptations towards muscle glycogen resynthesis and protein synthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828708","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The decision support systems (DSS) research literature within Information Systems (IS) is riddled with various overlapping definitions and approaches. Through an extensive literature review, this paper identifies key definitions, dimensions, and trends in the DSS literature and provides a unified classification. Based on the identified constructs, we identify a nesting challenge in DSS defined as the oversaturation of DSS approaches that occurs by continuously creating new approaches to cover specific use cases. We also argue that not all DSS approaches are comparable, as they address different aspects of decision support systems, with some defining application areas, while others focus on the technique or technology used. Through a discussion of the literature and the nesting classification, the paper draws on conceptual dimensions from business analytics (BA) research to define DSS approaches as domain-specific or technique-specific. From this point of departure, this paper calls for further research on integrating BA and DSS to enrich the application of DSS approaches in design and implementation. This literature review contributes to IS literature by showcasing a new perspective to create coherence within the DSS discipline.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Nikolaj Krebs","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776400"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business analytics","Decision support systems","Literature review","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"examing approaches and addressing the nesting challenge in decision support systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107199428/EXAMINING_APPROACHES_AND_ADDRESSING_THE_NESTING_CHALLENGE_IN_DECI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776400","ids":["itu-536f4292-8841-47d4-ab4f-e838e664c20e"],"keyword":["Business Analytics","Decision Support Systems","Literature Review","Machine Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-040256B38232E328E02982D3C04CCAE8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107199428/EXAMINING_APPROACHES_AND_ADDRESSING_THE_NESTING_CHALLENGE_IN_DECI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj Krebs","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"44aa2464-bb3c-413f-93fa-d5b56d85ec5c","name":"Pedersen, Nikolaj Krebs","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-536f4292-8841-47d4-ab4f-e838e664c20e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Examing Approaches and addressing the nesting challenge in Decision Support Systems.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776400","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Increasing digitalization means that many of our daily interactions happen within digital environments where they leave digital footprints in the form of trace data. Such digital trace data is often thought to generate insights by virtue of its immense scale. This focus on ‘big data’ tends to overlook the richness and complex characteristics of digital traces that opens new vistas for a multitude of computational analyses that generate new and high-resolution insights to digital environments. As such, paying attention to the characteristics of trace data allows for deep investigations of social-technical interactions in unprecedented detail. This chapter describes the process of digital trace analysis through four analytical activities aimed at identifying units of analysis, extracting categories, validating patterns and conceptualizing findings from digital trace data. It then shows how analytical activities can be applied to a given digital trace dataset to derive three ‘facets’ that each provide rich conceptualizations of social interaction with technology. It explains each facet and outlines ways to implement digital trace analyses that focus on facets relating to relations (network analysis), processes (sequence analysis) or semantics (text analysis).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Hukal, Philipp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-676159"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational qualitative analysis","Computational social science","Digital trace data","Network analysis","Sequence analysis","Topic modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rich facets of digital trace data","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-676159","ids":["cbs-7e6a9c32-f4fd-4848-b800-6c8df8654a82"],"keyword":["Computational qualitative analysis","Computational social science","Digital trace data","Network analysis","Sequence analysis","Topic modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7900EDBC1197F213F754D46D6D2A4A4D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Philipp","key":"hukalpau","last":"Hukal","locid":"339ca035-98ca-4ac7-a420-ccab91b36ed3","name":"Hukal, Philipp","orcid":"0000-0002-5928-0153","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Boyka","key":"simeonovapedh","last":"Simeonova","name":"Simeonova, Boyka","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert D.","key":"gallierspedh","last":"Galliers","name":"Galliers, Robert D.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/9781009106436.020","eisbn":["9781009106436"],"isbn":["9781009098878"],"pages":"247-267","place":"Cambridge","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Cambridge Handbook of Qualitative Digital Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-7e6a9c32-f4fd-4848-b800-6c8df8654a82"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Rich Facets of Digital Trace Data","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-676159","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Platform ecosystems have increasingly adopted self-organization to facilitate peer-to-peer decentralized collaboration. Just like any organizational system, decentralized platform ecosystems reorganize to update their alignment with the internal and external environments. However, unlike reorganizations of centrally managed ecosystems performed by the owners, reorganizations of decentralized platform ecosystems do not rely on formal authority. Instead, the network self-reorganizes to renew the structure, rules, and information to evolve. Despite the interdependence between the complementors (i.e., components) and the platform (i.e., core), little is known about how self-reorganizations influence complementor participation and engagement. In this study, we investigate all self-reorganization events (i.e., hard forks) that have taken place on Ethereum, a blockchain-based decentralized smart contract platform, to unpack how self-reorganizations of a complex decentralized platform ecosystem influence the participation of complementors. We find that, while self-reorganizations disrupt general complementor participation at transition, they facilitate the adaptation of complementor technical engagement over time. In addition, the relationship between self-reorganization and complementor participation is moderated by the nature of self-reorganization, i.e., the degree to which governance-related rule changes are involved. Our study integrates the organization design and platform literature and contributes to a deeper understanding of the interdependence of decentralized platform ecosystem evolution. In practice, our findings have implications for entrepreneurs building decentralized applications on top of decentralized platform infrastructures (e.g., smart contracts).","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hsieh, Ying-Ying","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689179"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Blockchain governance","Complementor Participation","Decentralized Collaboration","Platform ecosystems","Self organization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving a decentralized platform ecosystem self reorganization and complementor participation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-689179","ids":["itu-2f139c85-25d1-4a4a-98dc-7c93cbba06f8"],"keyword":["Blockchain Governance","Complementor Participation","Decentralized Collaboration","Platform Ecosystems","Self-Organization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B4441AB9E96F6C7CEE43998FCB0D421D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying-Ying","key":"hsiehpau","last":"Hsieh","name":"Hsieh, Ying-Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5465/amproc.2023.13610abstract","edition":"1","eisbn":["21516561"],"isbn":["00650668"],"issn":["00650668"],"publisher":"Academy of Management","series":"Academy of Management Annual Meeting Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Academy of Management Proceedings","volume":"2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2f139c85-25d1-4a4a-98dc-7c93cbba06f8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving a Decentralized Platform Ecosystem: Self-reorganization and Complementor Participation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689179","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Ingram Bogusz, Claire","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701234"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm School of Economics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the boundaries of fintech data driven classification and domain delimitation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5040/9781509963379.ch-001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701234","ids":["itu-b98507ba-915b-4693-99b1-aed46bda27ef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-242E31C8D832101E03AED3F74E9E6A11"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5040/9781509963379.ch-001","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102091082/9781509963379.ch-001.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm school of economics","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm School of Economics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, BUILD - Data Innovation Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"ingramboguszpau","last":"Ingram Bogusz","name":"Ingram Bogusz, Claire","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5040/9781509963379.ch-001","eisbn":["9781509963379","9781509963355"],"isbn":["9781509963348"],"pages":"3-24","place":"Oxford","series":"Swedish Studies in European Law","status":"p","title":"Fintech Competition: Law, Policy, and Market Organisation"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b98507ba-915b-4693-99b1-aed46bda27ef"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Boundaries of Fintech: Data-Driven Classification and Domain Delimitation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701234","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798559"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"åbent eller bare fragmenteret mobilisering gennem open source aktionsrepertoirer i den sociale blockchain bevægelse in studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk nordisk kontekst en forskningsantologi","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-798559","ids":["itu-d2ffbbec-4905-465d-ba1c-157ff722837d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-74A07DED0FD4F675E9BA403E54E56A3A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"IT University of Copenhagen","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d2ffbbec-4905-465d-ba1c-157ff722837d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Åbent eller bare fragmenteret? Mobilisering gennem open source aktionsrepertoirer i den sociale blockchain-bevægelse : In: Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst: en forskningsantologi","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798559","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Like any organizational system, platform ecosystems reorganize to update its alignment with the internal and external environments. However, unlike reorganizations of centrally managed platforms performed by the owners, reorganizations of decentralized platforms ecosystems do not rely on formal authority. Instead, the network self-reorganizes to renew the structure, rules, and information to evolve. Little is known about how self-reorganizations influence the participation of various types of networks. In this study, we investigate nine reorganization events on Ethereum, a blockchain-based decentralized smart contract platform, to unpack how self-reorganization related to hard forking influence participation in the development, validation, transaction, and complementor networks. We find that, while participation increases across all networks show a small increase after hard forking events, more complex dynamics are at play within each network that builds on delicate trade-offs between participation structure, configuration, and incentives. Our findings have implications for blockchain research as well as for start-ups building decentralized applications on top of decentralized smart contract platforms.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hsieh, Ying-Ying","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384334"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Blockchain participation","Decentralized platforms","Hard forking","Platform ecosystems","Self reorganization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reorganization and participation in decentralized platform ecosystems evidence from blockchain forking","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/83958335-1bdc-4b88-8e23-2f59a9a980bf/content","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384334","identifier":[{"id":"85152124395","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d113d377-ec14-4afe-8a64-7ae326e254af"],"keyword":["Blockchain participation","Decentralized platforms","Hard forking","Platform ecosystems","Self-reorganization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A5ABA1690660A4A63854EAF25DF85197"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/83958335-1bdc-4b88-8e23-2f59a9a980bf/content","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying-Ying","key":"hsiehpau","last":"Hsieh","name":"Hsieh, Ying-Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 56th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d113d377-ec14-4afe-8a64-7ae326e254af"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reorganization and Participation in Decentralized Platform Ecosystems: Evidence from Blockchain Forking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384334","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Blockchain systems allow for securely keeping shared records of transactions in a decentralized way. This is enabled by algorithms called consensus mechanisms. Proof-of-work is the most prominent consensus mechanism, but environmentally unsustainable. Here, we focus on proof-of-stake, its best-known alternative. Importantly, decentralized decision-making power is not an inherent feature of blockchain systems, but a technological possibility. Numerous security incidents illustrate that decentralized control cannot be taken for granted. We therefore study how key parameters affect the degree of decentralization in proof-of-stake blockchain systems. Based on a real-world implementation of a proof-of-stake blockchain system, we conduct agent-based simulations to study how a range of parameters impact decentralization. The results suggest that high numbers of initial potential validator nodes, large transactions, a high number of transactions, and a very high or very low positive validator network growth rate increase decentralization. We find weak support for an impact of changes in transaction fees and initial stake distributions. Our study highlights how blockchain challenges our understanding of decentralization in information systems research, and contributes to understanding the governance mechanisms that lead to decentralization in proof-of-stake blockchain systems as well as to designing proof-of-stake blockchain systems that are prone to decentralization and therefore more secure.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mueller-Bloch, Christoph","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Spasovski, Jason","Hahn, Jungpil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383520"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ESSEC Business School","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Centralisation","Decentralisation","Governance","consensus mechanism","decision making power"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding decentralization of decision making power in proof of stake blockchains an agent based simulation approach","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92564979/Mueller_Block_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383520","identifier":[{"id":"85138359889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9a14469f-94b8-427d-b117-b3abb8309872"],"keyword":["Blockchain","centralisation","consensus mechanism","decentralisation","decision making power","governance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D38CBE646B6E894150505DE50919C59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92564979/Mueller_Block_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4149460","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"essec business school","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ESSEC Business School","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"muellerblochpau","last":"Mueller-Bloch","name":"Mueller-Bloch, Christoph","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason","key":"spasovskipau","last":"Spasovski","name":"Spasovski, Jason","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jungpil","key":"hahnpau","last":"Hahn","name":"Hahn, Jungpil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0960085x.2022.2125840","issn":["0960085X","14769344"],"issn_org":["0960085X"],"journal":"European Journal of Information Systems","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138359889"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9a14469f-94b8-427d-b117-b3abb8309872"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding Decentralization of Decision-Making Power in Proof-of-Stake Blockchains: An Agent-Based Simulation Approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383520","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"As socio-technical processes related to digital innovation are increasingly connected and distributed across geographical, organisational, and temporal boundaries, the methods we use to study them must be adapted to accommodate the greater detail and scope of the phenomenon. Specifically, there is a need to operationalise methods for generating inductive theory of distributed digital innovation from digital trace data. An emerging stream of IS research on computationally intensive inductive theorising lays the groundwork for such methods. This paper builds on this foundation to develop a hands-on approach to operationalising grounded theorizing in computational analysis of digital trace data. The paper first conceptualises trace data of digital innovation as a new research context before articulating an approach to operationalising grounded theory in computational analysis of digital innovation. The application of the grounded computational analysis approach is then briefly illustrated in the context of digital trace data from an online social network before possible directions for further research are laid out.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384293"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational analysis","Digital innovation","Digital trace data","Grounded Theorizing","Socio Technical Processes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"grounded computational analysis a hands on approach to analysing digital innovation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://irisscis2022.cbs.dk/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Paper-5.-Jonas-Valbjorn-SCIS-2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384293","ids":["itu-ce8939a8-3a78-4f23-84a0-323ae13fbb10"],"keyword":["Computational Analysis","Digital Innovation","Digital Trace Data","Grounded Theorizing","Socio-Technical Processes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-949E27648587D8C129BC37B52E26143A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://irisscis2022.cbs.dk/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Paper-5.-Jonas-Valbjorn-SCIS-2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Thirteenth Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems (SCIS2022)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ce8939a8-3a78-4f23-84a0-323ae13fbb10"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Grounded Computational Analysis: A Hands-On Approach to Analysing Digital Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384293","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Abstract—The recent trends and challenges emphasize the need to exploit the potential of disruptive technologies in public administration. Accordingly, the main aim of the paper is to examine this issue over the last two decades. The results of bibliometric analysis on 3595 documents from Scopus reveal the growth of disruptive technologies research in public administration over time, especially in the last decade, as accelerated by several of the most relevant documents published in reputable journals such as Government Information Quarterly, Sustainable Cities and Society and Sustainability by several prominent authors. Most research has been conducted in the United States, followed by the United Kingdom and China and focused especially on artificial intelligence, followed by the internet of things, social media and blockchain, with the smart city being an important concept in disruptive technologies research in public administration. Finally, the results suggest that different public administration areas have different implications for disruptive technologies. The findings may be of benefit to not only the scientific community to serve as an important source for detecting associated research gaps but also to evidence-based policymaking to fully address the issues related to disruptive technologies in public administration in the future.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aristovnik, Aleksander","Ravšelj, Dejan","Umek, Lan","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381710"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Slovenia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Ljubljana"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Bibliometric analysis","Disruptive technologies","Public administration","Smart cities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mapping research trends on disruptive technologies in public administration a bibliometric approach","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.eventiotic.com/eventiotic/files/Papers/URL/f9523c35-3b96-4020-a382-70b90f0555ee.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381710","ids":["itu-1de27b08-b539-4e09-953a-e4f3b13d3862"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Bibliometric analysis","Disruptive technologies","Public administration","Smart cities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CF8455390AEF9CA238B573159329AB9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.eventiotic.com/eventiotic/files/Papers/URL/f9523c35-3b96-4020-a382-70b90f0555ee.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"si","key":"university of ljubljana","loc":["Slovenia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Ljubljana","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander","key":"aristovnikpau","last":"Aristovnik","name":"Aristovnik, Aleksander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dejan","key":"ravšeljpau","last":"Ravšelj","name":"Ravšelj, Dejan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lan","key":"umekpau","last":"Umek","name":"Umek, Lan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788685525247"],"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Information Society and Technology."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1de27b08-b539-4e09-953a-e4f3b13d3862"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mapping research trends on disruptive technologies in public administration: A bibliometric approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381710","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Increasingly advanced medicines have created monopolies in treatment areas with no viable options for generic substitution due to patent protection. As health care systems are increasingly under pressure to deliver health care improvements, costs become prohibitive as budgets are under pressure. To create financial flexibility, Danish regional authorities have over the period from 2009 until today developed, implemented, and gradually increased the use of a new model for analogue medicine substitution. The model introduces competitive tenders among patented medicines by declaring these medicines therapeutically equivalent in the treatment of specific diseases and thereby creating new opportunities for reducing annual medicine expenses. The model is based on enhanced collaboration among the health technology assessment (HTA) body, the procurement body, and the hospital owner, and it effectively covers medicine expenditure and cost-effectiveness while ensuring standardized treatments across hospitals and regions. The model is internationally unique in integrating several healthcare stakeholders and balancing their respective agendas to generate optimized outcomes for the healthcare system as a whole. However, some challenges persist, as the HTA process is resource and time consuming. Future research can show whether there are other challenges connected with the model.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Elisabeth","Hirsch, Niels Christian","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Ehlers, Lars Holger"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-691884"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Elisabeth"],"keyword":["Analogue medicines","Cost effectiveness","Pharmaceuticals","Stakeholder collaboration","Substitution"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DLI Market Intelligence"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the analogue substitution model introducing competition in the absence of generic substitution in danish hospitals","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.healthpol.2022.05.018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-691884","identifier":[{"id":"35728981","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85132913506","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fbb7e1a0-01c0-4434-9ed2-de4715114ec0","itu-9dd1fde1-5ecd-410f-a84a-da7a68e95ce7"],"keyword":["Analogue medicines","Cost-effectiveness","Pharmaceuticals","Stakeholder collaboration","Substitution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9D8CB1B39547F6C2DC27B07244FD5D4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0168851022001324?CMX_ID=&SIS_ID=&dgcid=STMJ_AUTH_SERV_PUBLISHED&utm_acid=124603232&utm_campaign=STMJ_AUTH_SERV_PUBLISHED&utm_in=DM265225&utm_medium=email&utm_source=AC_#!","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.healthpol.2022.05.018","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DLI Market Intelligence"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Healthcare Improvements"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Nordic Institute of Health Economics A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Elisabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Christian","key":"hirschpau","last":"Hirsch","name":"Hirsch, Niels Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Holger","key":"ehlerspau","last":"Ehlers","locid":"2ceddc99-bbe0-4721-8040-b4253e22468f","name":"Ehlers, Lars Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-6512-5566","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35728981"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.healthpol.2022.05.018","issn":["01688510","18726054"],"issn_org":["01688510"],"issue":"9","journal":"Health Policy","pages":"844-852","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Health Policy","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132913506"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","nordic institute of health economics a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fbb7e1a0-01c0-4434-9ed2-de4715114ec0","itu-9dd1fde1-5ecd-410f-a84a-da7a68e95ce7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Analogue Substitution Model: Introducing Competition in the Absence of Generic Substitution in Danish Hospitals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-691884","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Blockchain social movement not only opposed the economic system in the post-2009 financial crisis years, it provided a tangible technological alternative, built in computer code and using Open Source (OS) principles. The social movement mobilized using familiar OS structures and activities as action repertoires. Although this openness encouraged mobilization, this ran the risk of losing control, as individuals used the OS code for their own purposes, outside the scope of the social movement. The use of OS action repertoires provided ways to coordinate, vent and build consensus. Further, the resulting dissent, when it occurred made the movement more relevant by extending the movement and mobilizing individuals in complementary areas, driven by economic incentives. The OS repertoire of open entrepreneurship also facilitated mobilization, making the movement more influential.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ingram Bogusz, Claire","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383136"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","title":"Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm School of Economics"],"keyword":["Action repertoires","Blockchain social movement","Open Source OS principles","Open entrepreneurship","Post 2009 financial crisis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"open or just fragmented mobilization through open source action repertoires in the social movement of bitcoin","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10125/71390","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383136","ids":["itu-80060fdb-b029-4e80-b46a-6c82cfd1dc12"],"keyword":["Action repertoires","Blockchain social movement","Open Source (OS) principles","Open entrepreneurship","Post-2009 financial crisis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-76A52D593D2B440D2F70C23AEEAF997A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85687384/0624.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10125/71390","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/bitstream/10125/71390/1/0624.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm school of economics","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm School of Economics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"ingramboguszpau","last":"Ingram Bogusz","name":"Ingram Bogusz, Claire","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9780998133140"],"publisher":"University of Hawai'i at Manoa","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 54th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-80060fdb-b029-4e80-b46a-6c82cfd1dc12"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Open or just Fragmented? Mobilization through Open Source Action Repertoires in the Social Movement of Bitcoin","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383136","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we demonstrate how IS researchers can leverage the richness captured in the digital traces of social interactions within digital environments. We do so by proposing an approach to qualitative computational analysis based on 'faceting' of digital trace data. To illustrate how the faceting approach can be applied to data analysis, we describe the construction of three 'facets' inherent to digital trace data. Specifically, we show how researchers can focus on social structures (relational facet), sequences (processual facet), and meaning (semantic facet). We explain how to construct and work with each facet as a combination of analytical activity carried out by the analyst (data unit separation, data discretization, category validation, and conceptualization), as well as the analytical focus to which analytical activities are directed; the analysis of relations, processes, or semantics.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Hukal, Philipp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383615"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital trace data","Faceting Approach","Qualitative Computational Analysis","Semantic analysis","Social structures"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rich facets of digital trace data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3929483","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383615","ids":["itu-a16928ca-de03-4da4-9990-cdb5e8bf9361"],"keyword":["Digital Trace Data","Faceting Approach","Qualitative Computational Analysis","Semantic Analysis","Social Structures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-21EC46BC582C4DCE5A9A3543C888EAA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3929483","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philipp","key":"hukalpau","last":"Hukal","name":"Hukal, Philipp","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Cambridge University Press Handbook of Qualitative Research in the Age of Digitalisation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a16928ca-de03-4da4-9990-cdb5e8bf9361"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Rich Facets of Digital Trace Data","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383615","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Sveriges fintechsektor har skapat flera framgångsrika företag. I denna studie presenteras en första komplett kartläggning av de svenska fintechföretagen. Vidare presenteras en analys av åtgärder som skulle kunna skapa än bättre förutsättningar förinnovation och entreprenörskap parallellt med låga risker.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ingram Bogusz, Claire","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381983"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm School of Economics"],"keyword":["Entrepreneurship","Fintech sector","Innovation conditions","Risk mitigation","Swedish fintech companies"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"svensk fintech en kartläggning och analys av sektorn dess innovationskraft och utmaningar","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tillvaxtanalys.se/download/18.4edb065c1770000029e12acf/1611139766297/PM_2020_20_Svensk_fintech.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381983","ids":["itu-30d6e14b-6bd1-4a7d-a504-30234cdefaa5"],"keyword":["Entrepreneurship","Fintech sector","Innovation conditions","Risk mitigation","Swedish fintech companies"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D900FCE92CDD6C31A16222A9CAE5BDF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tillvaxtanalys.se/download/18.4edb065c1770000029e12acf/1611139766297/PM_2020_20_Svensk_fintech.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm school of economics","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm School of Economics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"ingramboguszpau","last":"Ingram Bogusz","name":"Ingram Bogusz, Claire","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"78","publisher":"Tilväxtanalys","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-30d6e14b-6bd1-4a7d-a504-30234cdefaa5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Svensk fintech : En kartläggning och analys av sektorn, dess innovationskraft och utmaningar","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381983","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The group I p21‐activated kinase (PAK) isoforms PAK1 and PAK2 are activated in response to insulin in skeletal muscle and PAK1/2 signalling is impaired in insulin‐resistant mouse and human skeletal muscle. Interestingly, PAK1 has been suggested to be required for insulin‐stimulated glucose transporter 4 translocation in mouse skeletal muscle. Therefore, the present study aimed to examine the role of PAK1 in insulin‐stimulated muscle glucose uptake. The pharmacological inhibitor of group I PAKs, IPA‐3 partially reduced (–20%) insulin‐stimulated glucose uptake in isolated mouse soleus muscle (P < 0.001). However, because there was no phenotype with genetic ablation of PAK1 alone, consequently, the relative requirement for PAK1 and PAK2 in whole‐body glucose homeostasis and insulin‐stimulated muscle glucose uptake was investigated. Whole‐body respiratory exchange ratio was largely unaffected in whole‐body PAK1 knockout (KO), muscle‐specific PAK2 KO and in mice with combined whole‐body PAK1 KO and muscle‐specific PAK2 KO. By contrast, glucose tolerance was mildly impaired in mice lacking PAK2 specifically in muscle, but not PAK1 KO mice. Moreover, while PAK1 KO muscles displayed normal insulin‐stimulated glucose uptake in vivo and in isolated muscle, insulin‐stimulated glucose uptake was slightly reduced in isolated glycolytic extensor digitorum longus muscle lacking PAK2 alone (–18%) or in combination with PAK1 KO (–12%) (P < 0.05). In conclusion, glucose tolerance and insulin‐stimulated glucose uptake partly rely on PAK2 in glycolytic mouse muscle, whereas PAK1 is dispensable for whole‐body glucose homeostasis and insulin‐stimulated muscle glucose uptake.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Møller, Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","Jaurji, Merna","Kjøbsted, Rasmus","Joseph, Giselle A","Madsen, Agnete B","Knudsen, Jonas Roland","Lundsgaard, Annemarie","Andersen, Nicoline Resen","Schjerling, Peter","Jensen, Thomas Elbenhardt","Krauss, Robert S","Richter, Erik A.","Sylow, Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463968"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","GLUT4 translocation","Glucose uptake","Insulin","Metabolism","Skeletal muscle","p21 Activated Kinases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin stimulated glucose uptake partly relies on p000000000021 activated kinase pak 000000000002 but not pak000000000001 in mouse skeletal muscle","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2019/12/16/543736.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-463968","identifier":[{"id":"85091043271","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7771197","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32844438","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-75f0ddc3-3679-4a71-84a8-8c3336093d7a"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","GLUT4 translocation","Glucose uptake","Insulin","Metabolism","Skeletal muscle","p21-activated kinases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EFBA81CD351828512859AFFD9BBBB286"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2019/12/16/543736.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Molecular Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"école polytechnique fédérale de lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"f8d5f61a-3e4b-4e4b-bee3-3d0be900cb6c","name":"Møller, Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0003-1885-0102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merna","key":"jaurjipau","last":"Jaurji","name":"Jaurji, Merna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"kjøbstedpau","last":"Kjøbsted","locid":"6a4c7845-3ae2-46e0-9a55-96d8574a5191","name":"Kjøbsted, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-0628-4994","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Giselle A","key":"josephpau","last":"Joseph","name":"Joseph, Giselle A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Agnete B","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Agnete B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Jonas Roland","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3bebd5f8-2b5c-4c65-9775-afe9e85d103a","name":"Knudsen, Jonas Roland","orcid":"0000-0002-5471-491X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annemarie","key":"lundsgaardpau","last":"Lundsgaard","locid":"247ea046-776b-4b22-816a-6368bcdf38e4","name":"Lundsgaard, Annemarie","orcid":"0000-0002-5584-2366","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicoline Resen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"668460c3-08c5-478e-8051-390adc8ea340","name":"Andersen, Nicoline Resen","orcid":"0000-0002-1512-2727","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Peter","key":"schjerlingpau","last":"Schjerling","name":"Schjerling, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Elbenhardt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"861af484-eb17-43a5-bbab-3d4f553a4537","name":"Jensen, Thomas Elbenhardt","orcid":"0000-0001-6139-8268","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Robert S","key":"krausspau","last":"Krauss","name":"Krauss, Robert S","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik A.","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lykke","key":"sylowpau","last":"Sylow","locid":"f86d592e-fb11-4ec7-a7b4-d63eb53f94c8","name":"Sylow, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-0905-5932","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32844438"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1113/jp280294","issn":["00223751","14697793"],"issn_org":["00223751"],"issue":"23","journal":"Journal of Physiology","pages":"5351-5377","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physiology","volume":"598"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091043271"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-75f0ddc3-3679-4a71-84a8-8c3336093d7a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Insulin-stimulated glucose uptake partly relies on p21-activated kinase (PAK)2, but not PAK1, in mouse skeletal muscle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463968","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The metaphor of the tanker and the speedboat has become almost apocryphal in management circles: large incumbent organisations are seen as too large and unwieldly to generate innovation, so they instead send out (and equip) speedboats, with the intention that they innovate and explore, and bring new ideas back to the tanker. However, this approach is very top-down and directed, and fails to harness one of the most powerful theorised qualities of digital artefacts, namely their ability to be generative, or be repurposed beyond the scale and scope originally intended (Zittrain, 2006).However, innovation in organisations large and small is also known to happen seemingly accidentally (Austin, Devin, & Sullivan, 2011; Shah & Tripsas, 2007). In an age of digital innovation characterised by as involving malleable and open-ended digital technologies (Kallinikos, Aaltonen, & Marton, 2013; Yoo, Henfridsson, & Lyytinen, 2010), and often leading to unanticipated, generative, outcomes, it is striking that we have such poor understanding of how micro-level digital technology diffusion leads to service innovation, whether in an incumbent organisation or otherwise.This paper adds to our understanding of service innovation in incumbent organisations, and structural changes to the organisation in particular, by developing a model of how micro-shifts accumulate to guide service innovation trajectories. Our study of GlobalBank focuses on how the introduction of a new mobile application, itself a small-scale innovation, eventually redefined frontline customer service in the bank’s branch network.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Ingram Bogusz, Claire"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381728"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm School of Economics"],"keyword":["Digital Artefacts","Innovation management","Micro Level Technology Diffusion","Organisational change","Service innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how micro shifts in technology knowledge practices and control structures transform service innovation trajectories","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85447965/Submission.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381728","ids":["itu-1eeccc6e-b93e-4bce-a628-8b3f95f71bdd"],"keyword":["Digital Artefacts","Innovation Management","Micro-Level Technology Diffusion","Organisational Change","Service Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1BA864D2FE04385200BE5A858F21D36F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85447965/Submission.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"stockholm school of economics","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm School of Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"ingramboguszpau","last":"Ingram Bogusz","name":"Ingram Bogusz, Claire","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1eeccc6e-b93e-4bce-a628-8b3f95f71bdd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HOW MICRO-SHIFTS IN TECHNOLOGY, KNOWLEDGE PRACTICES, AND CONTROL STRUCTURES TRANSFORM SERVICE INNOVATION TRAJECTORIES","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381728","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Muscle contraction stimulates skeletal muscle glucose transport. Since it occurs independently of insulin, it is an important alternative pathway to increase glucose transport in insulin-resistant states, but the intracellular signaling mechanisms are not fully understood. Muscle contraction activates group I p21-activated kinases (PAKs) in mouse and human skeletal muscle. PAK1 and PAK2 are downstream targets of Rac1, which is a key regulator of contraction-stimulated glucose transport. Thus, PAK1 and PAK2 could be downstream effectors of Rac1 in contraction-stimulated glucose transport. The current study aimed to test the hypothesis that PAK1 and/or PAK2 regulate contraction-induced glucose transport. Methods: Glucose transport was measured in isolated soleus and extensor digitorum longus (EDL) mouse skeletal muscle incubated either in the presence or absence of a pharmacological inhibitor (IPA-3) of group I PAKs or originating from whole-body PAK1 knockout, muscle-specific PAK2 knockout or double whole-body PAK1 and muscle-specific PAK2 knockout mice. Results: IPA-3 attenuated (-22%) the increase in glucose transport in response to electrically stimulated contractions in soleus and EDL muscle. PAK1 was dispensable for contraction-stimulated glucose transport in both soleus and EDL muscle. Lack of PAK2, either alone (-13%) or in combination with PAK1 (-14%), partly reduced contraction-stimulated glucose transport compared to control littermates in EDL, but not soleus muscle. Conclusion: Contraction-stimulated glucose transport in isolated glycolytic mouse EDL muscle is partly dependent on PAK2, but not PAK1.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Møller, Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","Nielsen, Ida L","Knudsen, Jonas Roland","Andersen, Nicoline Resen","Jensen, Thomas Elbenhardt","Sylow, Lykke","Richter, Erik A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-519368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contraction","Faculty of Science","Glucose uptake","Skeletal muscle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the p000000000021 activated kinase 000000000002 pak000000000002 but not pak000000000001 regulates contraction stimulated skeletal muscle glucose transport","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.14460","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-519368","identifier":[{"id":"32597567","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7322983","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85087024331","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d2c94a9f-1197-4711-8308-f3a7cd91472e"],"keyword":["Contraction","Faculty of Science","Glucose uptake","Skeletal muscle","p21-activated kinase"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49C1DBE16039AE734DCCE7F21446E666"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251694542/M_ller_et_al_Physiological_Reports_2020_Vol_8_12_e14460.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.14460","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Molecular Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"f8d5f61a-3e4b-4e4b-bee3-3d0be900cb6c","name":"Møller, Lisbeth Liliendal Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0003-1885-0102","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida L","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Ida L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Roland","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"3bebd5f8-2b5c-4c65-9775-afe9e85d103a","name":"Knudsen, Jonas Roland","orcid":"0000-0002-5471-491X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicoline Resen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"668460c3-08c5-478e-8051-390adc8ea340","name":"Andersen, Nicoline Resen","orcid":"0000-0002-1512-2727","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Elbenhardt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"861af484-eb17-43a5-bbab-3d4f553a4537","name":"Jensen, Thomas Elbenhardt","orcid":"0000-0001-6139-8268","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lykke","key":"sylowpau","last":"Sylow","locid":"f86d592e-fb11-4ec7-a7b4-d63eb53f94c8","name":"Sylow, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-0905-5932","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik A.","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32597567"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14814/phy2.14460","issn":["2051817X"],"issue":"12","journal":"Physiological Reports","paperid":"e14460","status":"p","title":"Physiological Reports","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087024331"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d2c94a9f-1197-4711-8308-f3a7cd91472e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The p21-activated kinase 2 (PAK2), but not PAK1, regulates contraction-stimulated skeletal muscle glucose transport","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-519368","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Given the ubiquity of digital technologies, and increased use of autonomous algorithms, it is likely that many of today’s social and organisational processes will one day include autonomous elements. The Bitcoin blockchain is likely the first case of an increasingly generative and autonomous way of organising—and one in which the blockchain itself, as a digital infrastructure, plays a crucial role in how, and which, organising objectives are realised. The specific properties of blockchain infrastructures—distribution of control, openness to manipulation, and generativity of the underlying source code—make it an ideal case to study patterns of what we call ‘selforganising’. This paper investigates the phenomenon of self-organising through a study of forking in the Bitcoin blockchain infrastructure between 2010 and 2016. It adds to the emerging body of research on digital infrastructures, and particularly blockchain infrastructures, by conceptualising forking as a pattern of self-organising in blockchain infrastructures, specifically involving: 1) the underlying infrastructure; 2) the scale of code changes; 3) individual objectives; and 4) collective adoption, whether specific or general. Thus, it shows how forking in blockchain infrastructures mediates between divergent organising objectives and existing capabilities, on the one hand, and generates self-organising on the other hand. It further contextualises these findings in extant work on digital infrastructures, offers a guide for designers of blockchain infrastructures and proposes the concept of ‘generative mirroring’ as a pattern wherein blockchain infrastructures and organising adaptively co-evolve.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Ingram Bogusz, Claire"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384875"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm School of Economics"],"keyword":["Bitcoin","Blockchain","Digital infrastructure","Forking","Generativity","Self organising"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self organising in blockchain infrastructures generativity through shifting objectives and forking","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/1jais.00566","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384875","identifier":[{"id":"85073743813","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f5054eca-e36c-42dc-9a3c-ef9f260c4d77"],"keyword":["Bitcoin","Blockchain","Digital infrastructure","Forking","Generativity","Self-Organising"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CE73935166527B54678EDD04AB3E5A56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/1jais.00566","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84029150/JAIS_3rd_Revision.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/jais/vol20/iss9/11/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"stockholm school of economics","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm School of Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"ingramboguszpau","last":"Ingram Bogusz","name":"Ingram Bogusz, Claire","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17705/1jais.00566","issn":["15583457"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of the Association for Information Systems","pages":"247-265","paperid":"11","publisher":"Association for Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Association for Information Systems","title_org":"Journal of the Association for Information Systems (JAIS)","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073743813"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f5054eca-e36c-42dc-9a3c-ef9f260c4d77"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Self-Organising in Blockchain Infrastructures: Generativity through Shifting Objectives and Forking","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384875","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Today’s business processes involve interactions with increasingly human-like algorithmic assistants based on artificial intelligence (AI). The prevalence of such anthropomorphized algorithmic assistants introduces a predicament for managers because it is often unclear to what extent and for which purposes algorithmic assistants can and will be trustedby customers and employees. In the near future, almost half of today’s work activities could be automated (Frey & Osborne, 2017), and as AI is increasingly changing how we work, and thereby the very fabric of our organizations (Faraj et al., 2018), it becomes ever more salient for managers to establish how human agents can interact with AI assistants in a reliable and trustworthy manner. In this paper, we examine how anthropomorphization of algorithmic assistants affect trust by human agents. Interestingly, our preliminary findings suggest that affective capabilities increase trust not only in the algorithm’s affective capabilities, but also in their cognitive capability. While the application of such AI-based algorithms increase efficiency in work processes and thereby economic output (Brynjolfsson & McAfee, 2014) and eliminates human bias in decision-making (McAfee and Brynjolfsson 2012), the long-term consequences of interactions between human and algorithmic agents in organizations are sparsely understood (Mankins & Sherer, 2014; Newell & Marabelli, 2015).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Crone, Tim","Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Shafeie Zargar, Mahmood","van den Hooff, Bart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381939"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deliotte","Vrije University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Algorithmic Assistants","Anthropomorphization","Artificial Intelligence AI","Human AI interaction","Trust in AI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trust me i am human how the anthropomorphization of ai is changing the human algorithmic relationship","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381939","ids":["itu-2d86ed05-7019-4adc-8c44-e6b40ac81a65"],"keyword":["- Algorithmic Assistants","- Anthropomorphization","- Artificial Intelligence (AI)","- Human-AI Interaction","- Trust in AI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2E3C68D30991301E02E30944C124505F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"deliotte","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Deliotte","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"vrije university amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vrije University Amsterdam","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"cronepau","last":"Crone","name":"Crone, Tim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahmood","key":"shafeiezargarpau","last":"Shafeie Zargar","name":"Shafeie Zargar, Mahmood","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bart","key":"vandenhooffpau","last":"van den Hooff","name":"van den Hooff, Bart","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2d86ed05-7019-4adc-8c44-e6b40ac81a65"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trust Me I am Human: How the Anthropomorphization of AI is Changing the Human- Algorithmic Relationship","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381939","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The promise of IoT technology to provide a ‘neural network for the physical world’ that opens new vistas for value creation has long been touted in information systems research. However, in many domains, this promise in large parts is still untapped due to clash between linear business models bound to singular organisations and distributed IoT infrastructures. In this paper, we propose a framework for conceptualising and quantifying value flows in IoT ecosystems and illustrate its potential usefulness for modelling the dynamics of IoT business models. We do so by presenting an illustrative system dynamics model of value flows in case of the Smart Office IoT ecosystem. Our research proposes venues of further research to model IoT value flows and thereby move closer to identifying specific IoT ecosystem value flows and their related business models.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Khan, Donya Sheikh"],"cuid":["S02-087.37-036342"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","end":"2019-06-14","place":"Stockholm-Uppsala, se","start":"2019-06-08","title":"27th European Conference on Information Systems","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Business model","Distributed Infrastructures","Ecosystems","Internet of Things IoT","IoT","IoT Business Models","System Dynamics Modeling","System dynamics","Value creation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"value flows in iot ecosystems towards an iot data business model","src":["dtu","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84029122/ECIS2019_IoT_value_revision.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-087.37-036342","ids":["dtu-a4dbb2a9-12a3-4971-af7f-3373beba1a7a","itu-a87849b8-52ab-491a-ad05-fd69341b0c7a"],"keyword":["Business model","Distributed Infrastructures","Ecosystems","Internet of Things (IoT)","IoT","IoT Business Models","System Dynamics Modeling","System dynamics","Value Creation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-244F275C0C66C57E5E5FFEBD3E45C681"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84029122/ECIS2019_IoT_value_revision.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Energy and Services"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Valbjørn","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3dac6e0e-2770-4c5e-b32a-d7750523516f","name":"Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-3366-5573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Donya Sheikh","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"f970adf4-14d7-4cdd-aa45-f5cdf6124f75","name":"Khan, Donya Sheikh","orcid":"0000-0001-7325-5627","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781733632508"],"pages":"1-10","publisher":"AIS Electronic Library (AISeL)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS) 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a4dbb2a9-12a3-4971-af7f-3373beba1a7a","itu-a87849b8-52ab-491a-ad05-fd69341b0c7a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Value Flows in IoT Ecosystems: Towards an IoT Data Business Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.37-036342","year":"2019","yearsub":2020}
{"abstract":"The Danish healthcare system is digitalising on all fronts. With the current state of big data, artificial intelligence (AI), and machine learning, the question is not whether these tools will be used to prioritise medication, but when and how. Managers responsible for future sales need to be aware that this provides a real competitive advantage for pharmaceutical companies that are ready to integrate data science in sales, marketing, market access, and medical affairs. This white paper outlines how to begin this transition and presents cases explaining how data science adds value to business operations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Jonas Valbjørn","Micheelsen, Arun","Lynne Hansen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689182"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Big data","Competitive advantage","Data Science Integration","Digitalisation in Healthcare","Healthcare management","Machine learning","Market access","Medical Affairs","Pharmaceutical Sales"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DLI Market Intelligence"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rise of data science in public healthcare and commercial pharma how public healthcare s rampup of data science solutions is an opportunity for well prepared commercial pharma organisations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dlimi.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/The-rise-of-data-science-in-public-healthcare-and-commercial-pharma.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689182","ids":["itu-4b7ccdae-0066-456a-83a9-9647cfc227f8"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Big Data","Competitive Advantage","Data Science Integration","Digitalis